      "event_at": "2026-03-18T14:20:00+03:00",
      "authored_at": "2026-03-18T16:00:00+03:00",
      "mime_type": "application/pdf",
      "text_content": "SYNTHETIC - NOT FOR CLINICAL USE\nCreatinine 1.42 mg/dL; eGFR 46 mL/min/1.73 m2; potassium 4.8 mmol/L; sodium 138 mmol/L; BUN 27 mg/dL. Results are final.",
      "storage_path": "cases/CASE-002/documents/DOC-002-13.pdf",
      "metadata": {
        "department": "Primary Care",
        "synthetic_label": "SYNTHETIC - NOT FOR CLINICAL USE"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "DOC-002-14",
      "patient_id": "SYN-002",
      "encounter_id": "ENC-002-06",
      "document_type": "specialist_consult",
      "title": "Nephrology consultation",
      "author": "Dr. Leila Morgan",
      "event_at": "2026-04-02T10:35:00+03:00",
      "authored_at": "2026-04-02T13:15:00+03:00",
      "mime_type": "application/pdf",
      "text_content": "SYNTHETIC - NOT FOR CLINICAL USE\nThe creatinine rise has partially improved after fluids. Possible contributors include volume depletion, NSAID exposure, and uncertain renin-angiotensin medication exposure. The available records do not establish which medicine was taken on each date. Recommend medication bottle review, avoid NSAIDs, and repeat renal panel.",
      "storage_path": "cases/CASE-002/documents/DOC-002-14.pdf",
      "metadata": {
        "department": "Nephrology",
        "synthetic_label": "SYNTHETIC - NOT FOR CLINICAL USE"
      }
    },
    {
